:''This article is about the Cat Unit. For the enemy, see [[Dhalsim (Enemy)]].''
'''Dhalsim''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that was implemented in [[Version 8.10 Update#Update 8.10.5|Version 8.10.5]] and can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Street Fighter Collaboration Event]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 516
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Dhalsim
|name2 = Dhalsim CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dhalsim CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Dhalsim, at first glance, may appear to have a great niche of crippling [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies, as they are notorious for having tough frontliners such as [[R.Ost]], [[Rain D.]] and [[Otta-smack-u]]. While it is true that he is able to weaken them from a safe range, he's not without competition, primarily being [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]], who has practically the same range as him, and is more spammable on top of having 100% Weaken uptime despite having Single Attack. It doesn't help that Dhalsim's closely spaced multi-hits does little to extent his ability uptime.

Even longer if range is needed, [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]] is another superior alternative due to having even more range, a significantly stronger Weaken and also being able to reach 100% uptime through [[Cat Combo]]s in True Form. This means that sadly, if you have Thaumaturge Cat or Driller Cat, you're likely never going to need or want to use Dhalsim. Outside of traitless threats, he is of little to no utility due to having low range and stats.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Midranger}}

